{{Short description|Football tournament details}}
{{distinguish|1974 FIFA World Cup Group 1}}
{{more citations needed|date=March 2026}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
Group A was one of two groups in the second group stage of the [[1974 FIFA World Cup]] finals. It was the first time that this stage of the competition (equivalent to the quarter-finals) was played in a group format.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Csató |first1=László |last2=Kiss |first2=László Marcell |last3=Szádoczki |first3=Zsombor |title=The allocation of FIFA World Cup slots based on the ranking of confederations |journal=Annals of Operations Research |date=12 June 2024 |volume=344 |issue=1 |pages=153–173 |doi=10.1007/s10479-024-06091-5 |url=https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-024-06091-5 |language=en |issn=1572-9338}}</ref> Matches were played in three cities ([[Dortmund]], [[Gelsenkirchen]] and [[Hanover]]) between 26 June and 3 July 1974. The group was composed of the winners of [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 1|Groups 1]] and [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 3|3]] from the first group stage ([[East Germany national football team|East Germany]] and [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]]), and the runners-up of [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 2|Groups 2]] and [[1974 FIFA World Cup Group 4|4]] ([[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] and [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]]).<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/74full.html |title=World Cup 1974 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

The Netherlands won the group after winning all three of their matches to qualify for the [[1974 FIFA World Cup Final|final]], while Brazil won their matches against East Germany and Argentina to finish in second place and qualify for the match for third place. East Germany and Argentina drew their match to finish level on one point, but East Germany's superior goal difference meant they finished the higher of the two.<ref name="fifastudy">{{cite web |title=FIFA World Cup 1974 Final Competition Technical Study |url=http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/afdeveloping/technicaldevp/50/09/65/wc_74_tr_312.pdf |publisher=FIFA |access-date=3 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111220060217/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/afdeveloping/technicaldevp/50/09/65/wc%5f74%5ftr%5f312.pdf |archive-date=20 December 2011 |pages=57–62}}</ref>

==Qualified teams==
The winners of Group 1 and 3 and the runners-up of Group 2 and 4 qualified for Group A of the second round.

